WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.185
Welcome. This is your ten-day plan for digraphs: two letters that make one new sound.

2
00:00:05.635 --> 00:00:08.973
Here is a word with two letters that team up and make one sound.

3
00:00:12.276 --> 00:00:13.268
The word is ship.

4
00:00:14.168 --> 00:00:21.921
The goal of this plan is a child who finds the two letters that make one sound, and reads words with them that were never seen before.

5
00:00:22.521 --> 00:00:28.208
That is the goal. It is not a promise. Day ten is a check, and it shows you where your child is.

6
00:00:29.008 --> 00:00:32.939
This plan is for a child who reads short words, like cat and hop.

7
00:00:33.389 --> 00:00:37.339
Often the child says the two letters of a pair apart, one sound each.

8
00:00:37.789 --> 00:00:40.335
Or stops at words like chin, this and ring.

9
00:00:40.785 --> 00:00:47.823
It is a normal step. Until now, every letter had its own sound. In a pair, two letters make one new sound.

10
00:00:48.273 --> 00:00:51.338
So this plan teaches one move. Find the pair first.

11
00:00:51.788 --> 00:00:56.292
Here is what is inside. Ten days. One page a day, about ten minutes.

12
00:00:56.692 --> 00:01:01.837
Day one is a short check. It shows you where to start. Day ten shows you what changed.

13
00:01:02.287 --> 00:01:07.544
Every day has a short video like this one, for you. It shows you what to do before you do it.

14
00:01:08.144 --> 00:01:13.310
Days two, three and four teach three pairs, one a day. The easiest to hear comes first.

15
00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:17.878
Day five is a halfway check. It tells you to go on, or to go back.

16
00:01:18.328 --> 00:01:20.992
Days six and seven teach the rest of the pairs.

17
00:01:21.442 --> 00:01:24.123
Then all of them mixed, and on day nine a story.

18
00:01:24.573 --> 00:01:29.406
Some days will need a second try. Doing a page twice is not falling behind.

19
00:01:30.006 --> 00:01:34.350
When a word goes wrong, do not say the word. Say the same words, every time.

20
00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.879
Two letters, one sound. Find the pair. Then wait.

21
00:01:38.779 --> 00:01:45.266
Here is how each day works. First, watch that day's video. Scan the code on the page with your phone.

22
00:01:45.716 --> 00:01:51.630
Then read the yellow box at the top of the page. It gives you three short steps, with the words to say.

23
00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:55.228
Do the first job together. That takes about two minutes.

24
00:01:55.678 --> 00:01:59.996
Then your child carries on with the page, and reads three things to you at the end.

25
00:02:00.446 --> 00:02:05.291
On five of the days your child has a track to listen to. You press play and step away.

26
00:02:06.091 --> 00:02:11.218
You need the printed pages, a pencil, crayons, and scissors for the cards on day two.

27
00:02:11.668 --> 00:02:16.756
When you are ready, start with day one. It is a short check, and it takes about four minutes.
